>On the other hand, I once consumed acid blob meat out of a tin, but it
>wasn't poisonous - I just got greasy fingers! I can't remember whether I
>was poison resistant or not - how is it really?
>

You can tin any corpse... whether spoiled or poisonous or acidic (although
you can not tin a partially eaten corpse).
The end result produces a tin of food which will be niether poisonous,
spoiled nor acidic. Although you might occassionaly get nauseous (but that's
no big deal, and a uni horn will fix you up proper)
This is great, since you can then eat undead corpses (ie: giant mummys,
giant zombies, et al) just by tinning them, then eating the tin.
Always keep a tinning kit in your BoH. =)

